That was a live demo.

00:34:16.193 --> 00:34:17.360
I was actually watching him.

00:34:17.360 --> 00:34:19.679
He did hit Refresh
button a couple times.

00:34:19.679 --> 00:34:20.540
My heart was racing.

00:34:20.540 --> 00:34:21.630
That was probably the
most exciting thing

00:34:21.630 --> 00:34:22.922
I'll see at a Cloud conference.

00:34:22.922 --> 00:34:25.250
[LAUGHTER]

00:34:25.250 --> 00:34:27.165
But with that, I
wanted to highlight--

00:34:27.165 --> 00:34:28.790
if it were Fabrizio
speaking, he wanted

00:34:28.790 --> 00:34:32.239
to highlight three big
things that Viant did

00:34:32.239 --> 00:34:33.980
in this particular scenario.

00:34:33.980 --> 00:34:36.380
One, in the first
slide, they showed

00:34:36.380 --> 00:34:39.409
that they had a very, very
extended cloud footprint.

00:34:39.409 --> 00:34:42.350
And they said, we no longer
want to manage infrastructure.

00:34:42.350 --> 00:34:46.030
That was the first step, no
longer manage that headache.

00:34:46.030 --> 00:34:48.409
Two, they created
an interface to make

00:34:48.409 --> 00:34:51.770
data accessible to their
entire organization.

00:34:51.770 --> 00:34:54.170
One of the more powerful
insights from that presentation

00:34:54.170 --> 00:34:57.090
was that it no longer
belonged to data scientists.

00:34:57.090 --> 00:34:58.340
It belonged to business users.

00:34:58.340 --> 00:35:00.290
It belonged to all
kinds of people

00:35:00.290 --> 00:35:03.880
that no longer needed to work
with the data scientists.

00:35:03.880 --> 00:35:07.640
And then, three, they're able
to extend the power of BigQuery

00:35:07.640 --> 00:35:10.193
with the rest of the
Google Cloud Platform.

00:35:10.193 --> 00:35:12.110
The most powerful thing
about that second demo

00:35:12.110 --> 00:35:15.020
was that it was now
using the machine

00:35:15.020 --> 00:35:18.950
learning APIs to basically
generate metadata

00:35:18.950 --> 00:35:20.870
to associate with creatives.

00:35:20.870 --> 00:35:23.980
Instead of having to create a
completely different workflow

00:35:23.980 --> 00:35:26.180
in a completely different
application for customers

00:35:26.180 --> 00:35:31.290
to access another part of
the Google Cloud ecosystem,

00:35:31.290 --> 00:35:34.710
this particular tool they built
was built all on top of that.

00:35:34.710 --> 00:35:37.960
And when I've seen
successful data companies,

00:35:37.960 --> 00:35:40.820
it's companies that really bring
the power of different cloud

00:35:40.820 --> 00:35:43.870
technologies all
together in one place.

00:35:43.870 --> 00:35:46.840
So to summarize,
BigQuery doesn't

00:35:46.840 --> 00:35:48.970
have to be exclusively
used by your data teams.

00:35:48.970 --> 00:35:51.220
Again, to think
that it is as only

00:35:51.220 --> 00:35:55.810
the domain of data scientists
would be very short-sighted.

00:35:55.810 --> 00:35:57.400
The real power is
when you unlock

00:35:57.400 --> 00:36:00.550
that power for the rest
of the organization.

00:36:00.550 --> 00:36:03.700
You create tools like Magnus
or build your own tools,

00:36:03.700 --> 00:36:05.560
work with other partners.

00:36:05.560 --> 00:36:09.190
And then lastly, BigQuery
is a flexible and extensible

00:36:09.190 --> 00:36:12.400
platform, one that allows
you to basically take

00:36:12.400 --> 00:36:17.503
its compute power and apply it
in many different scenarios.

00:36:17.503 --> 00:36:19.420
I don't know if you guys
were paying attention

00:36:19.420 --> 00:36:22.010
to the specific numbers
that were being generated,

00:36:22.010 --> 00:36:26.410
but in the first demo,
I saw that one iteration

00:36:26.410 --> 00:36:32.150
was going through 300 gigabytes
within 10, 15 seconds.

00:36:32.150 --> 00:36:34.810
And there was 10 queries
being run in parallel.

00:36:34.810 --> 00:36:36.490
That's about 3 terabytes.

00:36:36.490 --> 00:36:37.780
And again, that data--

00:36:37.780 --> 00:36:41.260
that processing time
doesn't scale linearly.

00:36:41.260 --> 00:36:43.992
It goes exponentially faster.

00:36:43.992 --> 00:36:45.450
And that is a very
powerful insight

00:36:45.450 --> 00:36:48.750
to take away, to help
